            <ArticleTitle>Spontaneous choledochal cyst rupture in pregnancy with concomitant chronic pancreatitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>127-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12664-012-0286-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Choledochal cysts are rare cystic transformations of the biliary tree that are increasingly diagnosed in adult patients. We report here a case of spontaneous rupture of a choledochal cyst in a pregnant young lady with chronic pancreatitis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
